Original solutions to all three questions of the <University of Oxford> Part B <Introduction to representation theory course of the University of Oxford> examination, held on 29 May 2023. Source: https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/request_for_mathematics_examinat/response/3129786/attach/3/FOI%20202507%20740%20Data.pdf#page=212[released examination PDF, bundle pages 212–213; paper pages 1–2]. The original numeric, letter and roman numbering is retained. All <associative algebras> and <modules> below are unital; the <characters> in Questions 2 and 3 are those of finite-dimensional <complex representations>.

